            <h2>Route Overview: Seattle to Leavenworth</h2>

            <p>Traveling from Seattle to Leavenworth by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect the Pacific Northwest's largest urban hub with one of its most charming mountain getaways. This route provides passengers with a relaxed alternative to driving - especially popular for leisure travelers, outdoor enthusiasts, and weekend trips seeking a Bavarian-themed village experience. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the service offers comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and spectacular views through the Cascade Mountains.</p>
            <p>The route is served by Amtrak's Empire Builder, offering daily departures between Seattle's King Street Station and Leavenworth's Icicle Station. Compared to road travel on the winding US-2 highway, taking the train helps you avoid mountain driving stress. It delivers you straight to the edge of this Bavarian-style village without worrying about parking or winter road conditions.</p>
