            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Seattle to Leavenworth covers roughly 78 miles (125 km) across the Cascade Mountains and Wenatchee Valley, linking the Pacific Northwest's largest city with its most famous Bavarian-themed village. Although this isn't a high-speed rail corridor like in Europe, Amtrak's Empire Builder offers a steady and pleasant pace, often making the trip more enjoyable than a winding mountain drive - especially during winter months when Stevens Pass can be treacherous.</p>
