            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography</h2>
            <p>The Seattle-to-Leavenworth train route runs through the heart of the Cascade Mountains, traveling east from Puget Sound through the Snohomish River Valley and over the Cascade crest before descending into the Wenatchee Valley. Passengers get spectacular views of the Cascade Range, including Mount Index, Mount Stuart, and the Wenatchee Mountains, making the journey more than just transit - it's a relaxed and picturesque mountain experience.</p>
            <p>The route passes through key cities and towns, including Everett and Wenatchee, before reaching Leavenworth. Along the way, travelers can enjoy natural scenery, including dense evergreen forests, roaring rivers, dramatic mountain peaks, and the transition from western Washington's rain-soaked landscape to the drier, sunnier climate of the Wenatchee Valley.</p>
