            <h2>Step-by-Step Journey Experience</h2>
            <p>Understanding the full journey from Seattle to Leavenworth can make your travel experience smoother and more predictable. Here's what to expect from station arrival to reaching your destination.</p>
            <h2>Arrival at the Station in Seattle</h2>

            <p>Most trains to Leavenworth depart from Seattle King Street Station, conveniently located near downtown Seattle.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Recommended Arrival:</b> 30-45 minutes before departure (Empire Builder is a long-distance train with more complex boarding).</li>
                <li><b>Facilities: </b>Ticket counters, waiting areas, restrooms, restaurants, baggage services, and paid parking.</li>
                <li><b>Architecture: </b>The station features beautiful Beaux-Arts architecture with ornate ceilings and chandeliers - worth arriving early to appreciate.</li>
                <li><b>Signage:</b> Platforms and departure boards are clearly marked for easy navigation.</li>
                <li><b>Transit Access:</b> Easily reachable via Link Light Rail (1 Line to Sea-Tac Airport), King County Metro buses, streetcar, and rideshare services.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2> Boarding Process</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Platforms are usually announced 20-30 minutes before departure.</li>
                <li>Boarding is organized, with clearly marked coach and sleeper cars.</li>
                <li>No airport-style security checks, making the process relatively quick.</li>
                <li>Sleeper car passengers enjoy priority boarding and immediate access to their private rooms.</li>
                <li>Staff are typically friendly and helpful with luggage, ski equipment, and gear storage questions.</li>
                <li>The Empire Builder is a long-distance train, so boarding is more deliberate than in regional services.</li>
            </ul>

